OneTimeUseIdPolicy::checkAction
├── given the configId was never initialized
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED for a burn and for any other op
├── given the call is the session's own well-formed burn op and the id is unspent and unexpired
│   ├── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS
│   ├── it should burn the id durably at once and emit IdConsumed
│   ├── when the burn is a consume
│   │   └── it should nominate no settlement
│   └── when the burn is a consumeFor
│       └── it should nominate the witness for the settling check
├── given the session's burn was validated earlier in this transaction
│   ├── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS for every other op, across batches
│   ├── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED for a second consume
│   ├── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED for a consumeFor after a consume (no nomination)
│   ├── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED for a second consumeFor and keep the first nomination
│   └── given another action slot pins the same id
│       ├── it should refuse that slot's burn
│       └── it should admit that slot's other ops
├── given no burn was validated in this transaction
│   ├── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED for every op
│   ├── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED when only another session's burn was validated
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED when the burn was validated under another multiplexer
│       └── and that burn should not spend this multiplexer's record
├── given the burn happened in an earlier transaction
│   ├── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED for every op
│   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED for another burn
├── given the call targets this policy with calldata shorter than a selector
│   └── it should fail closed and return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given the call targets this policy and the selector is consume or consumeFor
│   ├── when the id argument names ANOTHER session's id
│   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED and spend nothing
│   ├── when the op carries value
│   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
│   └── when the calldata is malformed or truncated
│       └── it should fail closed and return VALIDATION_FAILED
├── given the call targets this policy with any other selector
│   └── it should be a plain execution: refused before the burn, admitted after it
├── given the call is unrelated to this policy
│   └── when the session's burn led the batch
│       └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS
├── given the call is a Paymaster gas-refund callback (callbackAllowMaxAmount)
│   ├── when no burn led the batch
│   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED
│   ├── when the burn led and no callback was admitted yet in this transaction
│   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS once
│   ├── when a callback was already admitted in this transaction
│   │   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED for any target
│   └── it should bound the callback per (multiplexer, account, id)
└── given a deadline is pinned
    ├── when the deadline is in the future
    │   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS
    ├── when the current timestamp equals the deadline
    │   └── it should return VALIDATION_SUCCESS (inclusive)
    ├── when the deadline has passed
    │   ├── it should refuse the session's own burn op and spend nothing
    │   ├── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED for every other op
    │   └── it should return VALIDATION_FAILED even while the id is unburned
    └── when the deadline is zero
        └── it should never expire
